828 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186573631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573828 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "97bf5f88-079c-5c19-bc43-d82b428624e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186573625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573863 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb272fdc-0f82-5948-ba90-fb672bed1ac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $4$ is even, **then** $5$ is odd." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "125cbfce-91f0-5374-bd89-78fd1d13de57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573872 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $4$ is even.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $5$ is odd.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $5$ is odd, then $4$ is even." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** you do not go to work, **then** you do not get your salary." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e17e456-5cfd-52c7-99bf-b5bb8d3b9d9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573899 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You do not go to work.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You do not get your salary.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ You go to work.\n\n- $¬B:$ You get your salary.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you get your salary, then you go to work." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it doesn't rain, **then** Robert goes for a walk." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc18945c-2d46-5692-9a78-27019da5591c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573918 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It doesn't rain.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ Robert goes for a walk.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It rains.\n\n- $¬B:$ Robert doesn't go for a walk.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it rains, then Robert doesn't go for a walk." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** there are no clouds in the sky, **then** it is not raining." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ecab2b8f-98e3-5f6d-b4a6-b5491b118c68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573941 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ There are no clouds in the sky.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not raining.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not raining, then there are no clouds in the sky." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
